# EdminBoost Features

## Adding a Feature

1. Create `includes/features/class-edminboost-{name}.php` extending `EDMINBOOST_Feature_Base`.
2. Set `$id`, `$name`, `$description` on the class.
3. Implement `register_hooks()` — caller only invokes when `is_enabled()` is true.
4. Register in `EDMINBOOST_Features::load_features()` (`require_once` + `$feature_classes` array).
5. Add defaults in `EDMINBOOST_Feature_Settings::get_defaults()`.
6. Add enable logic in `EDMINBOOST_Feature_Settings::is_enabled()` (delegated by `EDMINBOOST_Settings::is_feature_enabled()`; `edminboost_is_feature_enabled` filter).
7. Add sanitization in `EDMINBOOST_Feature_Settings::sanitize()` (delegated by `EDMINBOOST_Settings::sanitize()`).
8. Add settings UI in `admin/partials/edminboost-feature-fields.php` under the correct `$section` (`productivity`, `security`, or `performance`).

## Feature Class Pattern

```php
class EDMINBOOST_My_Feature extends EDMINBOOST_Feature_Base {

	protected $id          = 'my_feature';
	protected $name        = 'My Feature';
	protected $description = 'What this feature does.';

	public function register_hooks() {
		add_action( 'admin_init', array( $this, 'init' ) );
	}
}
```

## Rules

- Command Center live admin bar (`EDMINBOOST_Command_Center_Bar`) is **not** a feature module — do not add it to `EDMINBOOST_Features`. See `edminboost-command-center.mdc`.
- Feature IDs: unique `snake_case` matching the `features` settings key.
- Read settings via `EDMINBOOST_Settings::get_feature_settings( $this->get_id() )` — not `get_option()`.
- Register hooks only in `register_hooks()`; no side effects in the constructor.
- Scope hooks to admin unless explicitly broader (e.g. `disable_emojis` uses admin hooks only).
- Skip plugin screens when a feature would interfere with its own UI — use `EDMINBOOST_Admin::PAGE_SLUG`.
- Prefer WordPress APIs over inline CSS/JS; inline styles only when justified (`EDMINBOOST_Hide_Notices`).
- For settings UI labels, expose static helpers (e.g. `get_widget_labels()`, `get_option_labels()`).

## Enable Logic Types

| Type | Examples | `is_feature_enabled()` behavior |
|------|----------|--------------------------------|
| Boolean flag | `hide_admin_notices`, `disable_xmlrpc` | truthy option value |
| Sub-key array | `dashboard_widgets`, `rest_api_hardening` | any sub-key enabled |
| Structured + text | `admin_footer` | `enabled` + non-empty `text` |
| Structured + scope | `disable_emojis` | `enabled` + `scope` (`admin`, `frontend`, `both`) |
| Structured + post types | `post_duplicator`, `disable_comments`, `post_order` | `enabled` + selected post types |

Sidebar hide/reorder lives in Menu Studio (`command_center.menu_studio`), not the feature registry — see `edminboost-command-center.mdc`. Admin bar cleanup toggles live in Appearance (`command_center.behavior`), not the feature registry — legacy `features.admin_bar` migrates on read.

## Feature Pages

| Page | Partial | `$section` |
|------|---------|------------|
| Productivity | `edminboost-productivity-page.php` | `productivity` |
| Security | `edminboost-security-page.php` | `security` |
| Performance | `edminboost-performance-page.php` | `performance` |

Shared fields: `admin/partials/edminboost-feature-fields.php` on Productivity, Security, and Performance pages. Settings page (`edminboost-settings-page.php`) is JSON backup/import only.

## Current Features

### Productivity

| ID | Class | Hooks |
|----|-------|-------|
| `hide_admin_notices` | `EDMINBOOST_Hide_Notices` | `admin_enqueue_scripts` (inline CSS; preserves error/warning notices) |
| `hide_screen_help` | `EDMINBOOST_Hide_Screen_Help` | `admin_head` (hides Screen Options + Help tabs) |
| `dashboard_widgets` | `EDMINBOOST_Dashboard` | `wp_dashboard_setup` (99), `admin_init` |
| `admin_footer` | `EDMINBOOST_Admin_Footer` | `admin_footer_text` |
| `post_duplicator` | `EDMINBOOST_Post_Duplicator` | `post_row_actions`, `page_row_actions`, `admin_action_edminboost_duplicate_post` |
| `classic_widgets` | `EDMINBOOST_Classic_Widgets` | `after_setup_theme` (disables block widgets) |
| `custom_admin_columns` | `EDMINBOOST_Custom_Admin_Columns` | `manage_*_posts_columns`, `manage_*_posts_custom_column` |
| `menu_duplicator` | `EDMINBOOST_Menu_Duplicator` | `admin_menu` (duplicate nav menu action) |
| `post_order` | `EDMINBOOST_Post_Order` | `pre_get_posts`, list table Order column + drag handle |

### Security

| ID | Class | Hooks |
|----|-------|-------|
| `disable_xmlrpc` | `EDMINBOOST_Disable_Xmlrpc` | `xmlrpc_enabled`, `wp_headers` |
| `disable_feeds` | `EDMINBOOST_Disable_Feeds` | `do_feed*` actions |
| `rest_api_hardening` | `EDMINBOOST_Rest_Api_Hardening` | `rest_authentication_errors`, `rest_index` |
| `login_redirects` | `EDMINBOOST_Login_Redirects` | `login_redirect`, `wp_logout`; Security UI: master `#edminboost_login_redirects_enabled` + dependent `#edminboost-login-redirects-options` (`.edminboost-dependent-section`; disabled until toggle on — see `initSecurityFeatures` in `admin-assets.mdc`) |
| `disable_comments` | `EDMINBOOST_Disable_Comments` | `admin_init`, `wp_before_admin_bar_render`, filters on comments |

### Performance

| ID | Class | Hooks |
|----|-------|-------|
| `disable_emojis` | `EDMINBOOST_Disable_Emojis` | `init` / `admin_init` per `scope` |
| `remove_asset_versions` | `EDMINBOOST_Remove_Asset_Versions` | `style_loader_src`, `script_loader_src` |
| `remove_dashicons_frontend` | `EDMINBOOST_Remove_Dashicons_Frontend` | `wp_enqueue_scripts` |
| `heartbeat_control` | `EDMINBOOST_Heartbeat_Control` | `heartbeat_settings` filter per context (`admin`, `editor`, `frontend`); Performance UI uses `.edminboost-select-rows` with setting help keys `heartbeat_admin`, `heartbeat_editor`, `heartbeat_frontend` |
| `disable_embeds` | `EDMINBOOST_Disable_Embeds` | `wp_enqueue_scripts`, `tiny_mce_plugins`, oEmbed filters |
